# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# internal-ax configuration. Copy to `.env` for local runs.
# In production these live in TWO layered Modal Secrets (see README "Deploy"):
#   internal-ax          (base)    ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY
#   internal-ax-project  (on top)  LANGFUSE_*, WEBHOOK_SECRET
# `scripts/bootstrap_modal.sh` writes the project secret from this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Langfuse harness project (dataset source AND trace sink) ---------------
# Note the v4 env var name is LANGFUSE_BASE_URL (not LANGFUSE_HOST).
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-...
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-...
LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://cloud.langfuse.com   # or https://us.cloud.langfuse.com

# --- Langfuse sandbox project (optional but recommended) --------------------
# What the AGENTS see as LANGFUSE_* inside their sandbox — a separate scratch
# project, so agent-created datasets/prompts/test traces don't pollute the
# harness project. Unset = agents share the harness project.
#SANDBOX_LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-...
#SANDBOX_LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-...
#SANDBOX_LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://cloud.langfuse.com

# --- Agent providers (base Modal secret only; not needed locally) -----------
# Claude Code authenticates with the Anthropic key; Codex with the OpenAI key.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Webhook auth ----------------------------------------------------------
# Langfuse remote-run webhooks carry NO signature/auth header, so we gate the
# endpoint with a shared secret passed as the `?token=` query parameter on the
# webhook URL you register in Langfuse. Leave unset — bootstrap_modal.sh
# generates one and appends it here.
#WEBHOOK_SECRET=
